\page options Options

```
Usage: vespercsi [OPTIONS]

VesperCSI - Wi-Fi Channel State Information Capture Tool

Capture Settings:
  -i, --interface-mac <mac>   [Required] MAC address of the capture interface
  -f, --frequency <freq>      Center frequency in MHz (e.g., 2412, 5180)
  -w, --channel-width <width> Channel bandwidth [20|40|HT40-|80|160]
  -F, --format <format>       CSI format [NOHT|HT|VHT|HESU]
  -r, --num-rx <num>          Number of RX antennas (1 or 2)
  -t, --num-tx <num>          Number of TX antennas (1 or 2)

Filtering Options:
  -s, --src-mac <mac>         Filter incoming packets by source MAC address
  -u, --unrestricted          Do not restrict capture to matched channel width and format

Output & Plugins:
  -o, --out <file>            Path to write raw CSI data
  -p, --plugin <path>         Path to load an external shared library plugin (.so)
  -P, --plugin-config <file>  Path to configuration file for the loaded plugin
  -c, --config <file>         Path to VesperCSI configuration file for extra functionality

Logging & Output Control:
  -l, --log <file>            Path to write application logs
  -v, --verbose[=level]       Enable verbose debug output (levels: 0, 1, 2)
  -q, --quiet                 Suppress all console output

Advanced & Miscellaneous:
  -d, --daemon                Run VesperCSI as a background daemon
      --netlink-buffer-instant-death  Crash immediately on netlink buffer overflow
      --ring-buffer-instant-death     Crash immediately on ring buffer overflow
      --debug-constants       Print internal debug constants and exit
  -h, --help                  Show this help message and exit
      --version               Show program version and exit
```
